# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Things that are deliberately NOT committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Drafts, strategy notes, scratch scripts, anything half-finished. Put it in
# `_private/` and it cannot reach a commit by accident.
#
# Why this exists: on 2026-09-16 a `git add -A docs/` swept an untracked
# open-core/licensing note into a commit and pushed it to the PUBLIC repo. It
# was removed from HEAD within minutes, but a commit in a public history is not
# something you take back -- undoing it means a force-push, which is a decision
# the author has to make, not a tidy-up.
#
# The rule that goes with the folder: stage files by NAME. Never `git add -A`,
# never `git add .`. An untracked file in this repo is a deliberate state.
_private/
